From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:41:19 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: simple: af: Skip frames without statistics

The software ISP fills the statistics only every kStatPerNumFrames
frames; on the others stats->valid is false and the variance is the
previous frame's. Agc, Awb and BlackLevel skip those frames. Af did not,
so it moved the lens on every frame and compared each new position with
a measurement taken at an old one.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 src/ipa/simple/algorithms/af.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/af.cpp b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/af.cpp
index a208ada5..d4f025dc 100644
--- a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/af.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/af.cpp
@@ -40,6 +40,10 @@ void Af::process(IPAContext &context,
 		 const SwIspStats *stats,
 		 [[maybe_unused]] ControlList &metadata)
 {
+	/* statistics come every kStatPerNumFrames frames, as for Agc and Awb */
+	if (!stats->valid)
+		return;
+
 	const double variance = stats->variance;
 	LOG(IPASoftIspAf, Debug) << "Focus stats: " << variance;
 	afAlgo_.process(context.activeState.af, variance);
